We need to find the number of stones each alien has after $N$ years.

Let's break down the timeline.
At year $k$ (where $1 \le k \le N$), the $k$-th alien becomes an adult.
The condition "every adult who has at least one stone" refers to the set of aliens who have already become adults.
Specifically, at year $k$, aliens $1, 2, \dots, k-1$ have already become adults. Alien $k$ is the one becoming an adult right now.
