The cost to increase the count of product $i$ from $x$ to $x+1$ is $(x+1)^2 P_i - x^2 P_i = (2x+1)P_i$.
This marginal cost is increasing with $x$. This is a classic property of convex functions.
We can think of this as having a set of items to buy.
For product $i$, the 1st unit costs $1^2 P_i - 0^2 P_i = P_i$.
The 2nd unit costs $2^2 P_i - 1^2 P_i = 3 P_i$.
